    "Universitas Gadjah Mada is forming a fact-finding team regarding the detention of students during recent demonstrations.",
    "Police officials have initiated an investigation into alleged ethics violations by three officers during the protests.",
    "Regional law enforcement leadership in Yogyakarta has been reorganized following the incidents on November 10."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Tensions in Yogyakarta escalated following a protest on November 10, which resulted in the arrests of four individuals, including students from Universitas Gadjah Mada. In response to allegations of procedural violations and the entry of security forces into university facilities, UGM leadership has announced the creation of a team to investigate the events. Authorities have stated that three police officers in the region are currently under disciplinary detention for alleged ethics violations committed during the protest. Furthermore, recent reports confirm leadership changes within the Yogyakarta regional police department. The university has publicly expressed its opposition to violence and urged that students involved in demonstrations not be confronted with intimidation. The situation remains a subject of ongoing administrative and institutional review to address concerns regarding the treatment of students and the conduct of security personnel during the unrest.",
